@baseUrl = https://localhost:7032
# Set userName, password, accessToken, staffUserName, staffPassword and staffRoleId
# in your HTTP client's private environment. Never commit real credentials/tokens.

### Login by UserName only
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{userName}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Current safe user information
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Admin creates staff (use actual allowed RoleId from your database)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{staffUserName}}",
  "password": "{{staffPassword}}",
  "roleId": {{staffRoleId}},
  "fullName": "Restaurant Staff",
  "email": null,
  "phoneNumber": null,
  "avatarUrl": null
}

### Logout current session; reuse of this token must return 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
